  "_withdrawn": {
    "popup-spin-to-win": "Withdrawn, not deferred. A wheel needs a per-visitor outcome, and the payload is baked into HTML the full-page cache serves byte-identically to every visitor — so either every segment's prize ships in the page source or none does (ADR 0025, \"no coupon minting, and not as a preference\"). One spin per visitor is a claim about a PERSON, and WConvert mints no visitor identifier (ADR 0017); wcv1 is a browser record, so a second browser is a second spin. And a stored outcome serves two purposes in two consent categories at once, which is the question ADR 0052 left open and ADR 0053 answers. This file is bundled advertising: a card for a design nobody can ever be given is a worse defect than one fewer card. See docs/adr/0053-the-spin-to-win-card-is-withdrawn.md, and do not re-add it without reopening ADR 0003 first."
  },
